      "romanization": "jāṇā · khāṇā · pīṇā · saundā",
      "gloss": "retrieve to go, to eat, to drink and the familiar sleeps form by ear",
      "script": "gurmukhi",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:6073bf5f7cc35b93",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "jāṇā; khāṇā; pīṇā",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *jāṇā; khāṇā; pīṇā*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਜਾਣਾ, ਖਾਣਾ, ਪੀਣਾ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already say ਕਰਦਾ, \"does\", and ਸੌਂਦਾ, \"sleeps\". Listen to the two middles: kar-dā runs straight into its ending, but saun-dā carries a nasal hum before it. The next lesson gives that hum to three verbs you use every day."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "to go",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *to go*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਜਾਣਾ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "to eat",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *to eat*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਖਾਣਾ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "to drink",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *to drink*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਪੀਣਾ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "sleeps, of a man",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *sleeps, of a man*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਸੌਂਦਾ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the four once more, slowly. Nothing new is needed yet."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PA-C211-janda",
      "sequence": 11510,
      "title": "ਜਾਂਦਾ, ਜਾਂਦੀ — goes, every day",
      "headword": "ਜਾਂਦਾ · ਜਾਂਦੀ",
      "romanization": "jāndā · jāndī",
      "gloss": "goes, every day: the present of ਜਾਣਾ for a man and for a woman",
      "script": "gurmukhi",
      "modality": "sight",
      "derivedModality": "sight",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "eyes-or-hands-step"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:09d73967fc279ce5",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "sight",
        "needs": [
          "your eyes or your hands for the steps that ask you to read, point, write or gesture"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your eyes, so it is not fully a driving lesson. You will want your eyes or your hands for the steps that ask you to read, point, write or gesture. You can listen to everything else now. I will say so again when we reach it, but leave this section until you have stopped: Guided Practice."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਜਾਣਾ, \"to go\", then ਸੌਂਦਾ, \"sleeps\". Then every day: ਰੋਜ਼."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: a stem that ends in a vowel",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Take -ਣਾ off ਜਾਣਾ and the stem ਜਾ ends in a vowel. Before -ਦਾ such a stem takes a nasal, the dot ਂ, as ਸੌਂਦਾ does:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਜਾ + ਂ + ਦਾ becomes ਜਾਂਦਾ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮੈਂ ਰੋਜ਼ ਸਕੂਲ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ। — maiṁ roz sakūl jāndā hāṁ. — I go to school every day (a man speaking)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਮੈਂ ਰੋਜ਼ ਸਕੂਲ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹਾਂ। — maiṁ roz sakūl jāndī hāṁ. — I go to school every day (a woman speaking)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending agrees with the one who goes, as in ਮੈਂ ਪੰਜਾਬੀ ਬੋਲਦਾ ਹਾਂ. The helper ਹਾਂ stays at the end."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "I go home every day, as a man",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *I go home every day, as a man*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਮੈਂ ਰੋਜ਼ ਘਰ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹਾਂ।."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "she goes to school every day",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *she goes to school every day*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say ਉਹ ਰੋਜ਼ ਸਕੂਲ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ।."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "ਜਾਂਦਾ",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: **ਜਾਂਦਾ**]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Point to the dot that brings the nasal."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "copy ਜਾਂਦਾ once",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: copy **ਜਾਂਦਾ** once]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Goes, of a man? (ਜਾਂਦਾ.) Of a woman? (ਜਾਂਦੀ.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
